  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal obligations for NAICS 611430, Professional and Management Development Training, total $355M for FY2026 to date. Award activity shows 1,856 awards so far, with an average award size of $191K. Year over year obligations are down 55.7%. Looking back across recent years, obligations were $908M in FY21, $874M in FY22, $974M in FY23, $1B in FY24, and $802M in FY25. The FY2026 total of $355M is the lowest point in the series provided. These numbers are contract obligations and the current-year totals are partial because they are fiscal year to date. That matters when you compare FY2026 to full prior years. Buyers are led by the Department of Defense at $175M, followed by the Department of the Interior at $51.3M and the Department of Homeland Security at $32.1M. The largest reported vendors for FY2026 to date are THE BOEING COMPANY at $61.5M and DEEP MILE NETWORKS LLC at $48.8M, with several other vendors receiving single-digit millions in obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed in spending in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Obligations for FY2026 to date are $355M, down 55.7% year over year. That compares with $802M in FY25 and earlier fiscal-year totals as high as $1B in FY24. The FY2026 total is a partial, fiscal year to date figure, so it is lower than full-year totals from prior years. Award volume so far is 1,856 awards with an average award size of $191K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the largest buyers and vendors this year?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer at $175M, followed by the Department of the Interior at $51.3M and the Department of Homeland Security at $32.1M. THE BOEING COMPANY is the top vendor at $61.5M and DEEP MILE NETWORKS LLC is second at $48.8M. Other notable vendors include LEIDOS, INC. at $19M and HIGHERECHELON, INC. at $13.4M."
      }
    ]
  },
